# GIT CONFIGURATION

## Git Config

- Git stores configuration settings.

- I can see configuration using:

    git config --list

- Global settings apply to my user account.

- Local settings apply only to a particular repository.

- Example:

    git config --global user.name "My Name"

- Repository-specific settings can be configured without `--global`.

